\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Scalar fields on group orbits}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{A sign attached to each vertex can favor agreement across an edge.
Flipping every sign preserves each agreement, even in a configuration
with many disagreements. Which features of the scalar field survive
averaging over configurations, and what changes when an external field
favors one sign?}

\p{The [orbit gauge–Higgs weight](fdip-010A) compares neighboring
values by transporting one along the intervening link. This allows the two endpoints
to change frames independently.}

\transclude{fdip-00ZU}
